St. Columba Parish
Guide to the Sacraments

Baptism
Parents who wish to have a child baptized should register with the parish office at least two months ahead.
The baptism preparation class is held on the second Sunday of each month at 11:45 am in the Kerrigan Room.
Parents attend one class before the first child is baptized. Godparents are welcome but not required to attend.
Please bring a copy of the child's birth certificate when you register.

Marriage
Couples should contact the parish office at least nine months before the wedding date.
A marriage preparation weekend is offered each spring and fall at the Wendover Retreat Center.

Anointing of the Sick
Call the parish office at any hour. After hours, the answering service will page the priest on call.

First Communion and Confirmation
Children prepare through the religious education program. See the religious education calendar for class dates.
